# `COPY . .` runs after `pnpm install`, so anything listed here would otherwise be
# copied over the image's own install. node_modules is the dangerous one: the
# host's copy holds platform-native binaries (rollup, esbuild) built for the
# developer's OS, which then fail inside Alpine. Every workspace has its own, hence **.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Mobile build state — the image only builds the web app.
apps/mobile/.expo
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local overrides are developer-specific and must never reach an image.
# `.env` itself is kept: it supplies the VITE_* fallbacks when a build arg is
# not passed.
**/*.local

.vscode
.idea
.claude
**/*.log

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
